.TH NCDU\-CLEAN 1 "September 2026" "ncdu-clean 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ncdu\-clean \- delete files found with ncdu, keeping a journal and a quarantine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ncdu\-clean browse
.RI [ options ]
.I EXPORT
.br
.B ncdu\-clean rm
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ PATH ...]
.br
.B ncdu\-clean log
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ncdu\-clean restore
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ RUN
.RI [ PATH ...]]
.br
.B ncdu\-clean list
.RI [ options ]
.I EXPORT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ncdu\-clean
works on an export made by
.BR ncdu (1)
(\fBncdu \-e \-o scan.json /path\fR).
It lets you browse the export, mark files and directories, and then choose what
to do with them: delete them, move them to a quarantine, or save the list.
The journal entry is written before the file is removed. Quarantined files
can be put back where they came from.
.PP
With an export, each path is checked against that export before removal.
A file whose size or modification time changed since the scan, or a directory
that gained files, is refused.
.B rm
without \fB\-\-export\fR skips this check and warns.
Paths at the top of the tree (\fB/\fR, \fB/etc\fR, \fB/var\fR, ...), the home
directory and the root of the scan are always refused.
Every action is simulated first; nothing is done without \fB\-\-yes\fR or an
explicit confirmation in the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B browse \fIEXPORT\fR
Browse the export like
.BR ncdu (1).
Mark items with Space, then press
.B x
to simulate the selection and choose: delete permanently, quarantine, or save
the list to a file.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" ", \-\-out " FILE
Keep the selection in
.I FILE
as you go, and reload it if it exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Journal to use.
.RE
.TP
.B rm \fIPATH\fR...
Check, then delete or quarantine the given paths (for scripts).
Simulation by default.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Really act.
.TP
.BI \-e " EXPORT" ", \-\-export " EXPORT
Check that nothing changed since the scan.
Without this option, that check is skipped.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Allow non-empty directories.
.TP
.BI \-\-trash " DIR"
Move into
.IR DIR / RUN /...
instead of deleting.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " FILE"
Read paths from
.IR FILE ,
one per line (\fB\-\fR means standard input).
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Paths are separated by NUL.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Journal to use.
.RE
.TP
.B log
Show the journal: date, action, size, path.
Options:
.BI \-\-grep " TEXT"
filters on the path,
.BI \-\-last " N"
keeps the last N lines.
.TP
.B restore \fR[\fIRUN\fR [\fIPATH\fR...]]
Without argument, list the quarantine runs with their state.
With a run identifier (or a prefix, or
.BR last ),
put its files back where they came from; with paths, put back only those.
Nothing is ever overwritten: if the destination exists, the file stays in the
quarantine and a conflict is reported; existing directories are merged.
Simulation by default; use
.B \-\-yes
to act.
Directories re-created on the way get default permissions.
.TP
.B list \fIEXPORT\fR
Flat list of the files of an export, biggest first, as
.IR size <TAB> path .
Options:
.BR \-\-dirs ,
.BI \-\-min\-size " SIZE" ,
.BI \-\-top " N" ,
.BR \-\-apparent ,
.BR \-0 .
.SH BROWSER KEYS
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " j / k
Move.
.TP
.BR Right / Enter ", " l
Open the directory.
.TP
.BR Left / Backspace ", " h
Parent directory.
.TP
.B Space
Mark or unmark the item (a whole directory if it is one).
.B [*]
is marked, and
.B [+]
is covered by a marked directory above.
.TP
.B x
Act on the selection.
.TP
.B c
Clear the selection.
.TP
.BR s ", " n
Sort by size, by name.
.TP
.B a
Switch between disk usage (space really taken, what you get back) and file
size (length of the content).
.TP
.BR ? ", " q
Help, quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ncdu\-clean/deleted.jsonl
Default journal (\fI/var/log/ncdu\-clean.jsonl\fR for root), one JSON object per
line and per file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ncdu\-clean/quarantine/
Default quarantine.
Moving files there does not free disk space.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NCDU_CLEAN_LOG
Journal to use when
.B \-\-log
is not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ncdu \-e \-o scan.json /var
ncdu\-clean browse scan.json
ncdu\-clean rm \-r \-e scan.json /var/tmp/old \-\-trash ~/q \-\-yes
ncdu\-clean restore
ncdu\-clean restore last /var/tmp/old/file.log \-\-yes
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if some path was refused, missing, in conflict or failed; 2 on
usage or input errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ncdu (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Thomas Lloancy
